# DrawSplay: lets members of the plugdev group set the kernel's EDID override list
# (drm.edid_firmware) without root. On KDE Plasma, DrawSplay shows the tablet on a spare,
# unplugged HDMI port as a monitor with the tablet's EDID (installed once, as root, in
# /lib/firmware/edid/drawsplay-*.bin), so Display Configuration offers the tablet's
# resolutions. The host adds its own entry only while the tablet uses the port and removes
# it afterwards; it never changes the entries it did not add.
#
# The parameter is global: a plugdev member could point any connector at any EDID file in
# the firmware directory, which can at worst give a monitor the wrong modes until the entry
# is removed or the computer restarts. Remove this file to keep the parameter root-only;
# DrawSplay then asks for a password each time it sets the entry.
ACTION=="add|change", SUBSYSTEM=="drm", KERNEL=="card[0-9]*", ENV{DEVTYPE}=="drm_minor", RUN+="/bin/sh -c 'chgrp plugdev /sys/module/drm/parameters/edid_firmware && chmod 0664 /sys/module/drm/parameters/edid_firmware'"
